First 2 hours with both inlets only:

\[
2\left(\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{20}\right)=2\left(\frac{5}{20}+\frac{1}{20}\right)=2\cdot\frac{6}{20}=\frac{3}{5}
\]

Remaining:

\[
1-\frac{3}{5}=\frac{2}{5}
\]

After the drain is opened, the net rate is:

\[
\frac{1}{4}+\frac{1}{20}-\frac{1}{6}
= \frac{15}{60}+\frac{3}{60}-\frac{10}{60}
= \frac{8}{60}
= \frac{2}{15}
\]

Time to fill the remaining \(\frac{2}{5}\):

\[
\frac{\frac{2}{5}}{\frac{2}{15}}=3 \text{ hours}=180 \text{ minutes}
\]

